By that standard, football is a roleplaying game. After all, you _can_
enter the field clad in togas, shouting "Eureka!"

The question is, though: what is your purpose in this game? In true
roleplaying games, it is developing your character by playing your role.
In football, it is kicking the ball behind the keeper. In NetHack, it is
bringing the amulet to the Astral plane. Roleplaying is not a _primary_
goal in the latter two games, even though you can bring them into it.
(In the same way, D&D is not an artifact-finding game, even though you
can certainly write scenarios in which that is the superficial goal of
the quest.)

